---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import GlitchText from '../components/GlitchText.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About TechFencing" description="Who made this, why, and what I'm trying to do.">

  <section class="hero-sm">
    <div class="container" style="position:relative;z-index:1;">
      <GlitchText text="About" tag="h1" class="page-title" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="flowing-line"></div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container about-content">

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2 class="glitch-hover" data-text="Who I Am">Who I Am</h2>
        <p>
          I'm a fan. That's it. I watched PewDiePie's tech videos — the Linux
          one, the de-Google one, the "I Fixed YouTube!" one — and decided to
          actually do the stuff he talked about. I'm logging it all and working
          through it as I go.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm not a cybersecurity expert. I'm not a Linux veteran. I'm someone
          who was tired of feeling like a product and decided to do something about
          it. This site is my attempt to organize everything into one place so you
          don't have to piece it together yourself.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2 class="glitch-hover" data-text="Why This Exists">Why This Exists</h2>
        <p>
          In March 2026, PewDiePie published "I Fixed YouTube!" and coined the term
          <strong>"tech fencing"</strong> — the practice of building barriers between
          yourself and the technology designed to exploit your attention and data.
        </p>
        <p>
          The video resonated. People wanted to do it. But the information was spread
          across multiple videos, with specific tool names dropped casually and setup
          details easy to miss if you weren't paying attention.
        </p>
        <p>
          This site gathers all of that into one place. Every recommendation is
          sourced from PewDiePie's videos with citations and timestamps. Every guide
          includes honest downsides. Every page is written for someone who might be
          doing this for the first time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2 class="glitch-hover" data-text="What I Believe">What I Believe</h2>
        <ul class="belief-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Privacy is a default, not a stance.</strong> You don't need a
            reason to not want strangers reading your messages. It's not about
            having something to hide — it's about having something that's yours.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Progress over perfection.</strong> Switching your browser is
            better than doing nothing. You don't need to install Linux on day one.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Honesty over evangelism.</strong> If something sucks, I say so.
            If PewDiePie still uses Google Maps, I mention it. I'm not here to
            sell you on a lifestyle — I'm here to give you information.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Learning is the point.</strong> I'm still figuring this out.
            Every guide is written by someone who recently went through the same
            process. If I got something wrong, that's a feature — it means I'm
            still learning.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="about-block">
        <h2 class="glitch-hover" data-text="Disclaimers">Disclaimers</h2>
        <ul class="disclaimer-list">
          <li>This site is <strong>not affiliated with PewDiePie</strong>. I'm a fan who organized his publicly available content.</li>
          <li>I note when products are <strong>PewDiePie sponsors</strong> (Hostinger, Incogni) so you can factor that into your decisions.</li>
          <li>I don't run Google Analytics or any third-party tracking. <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> is auto-injected by the hosting platform — it's cookie-free, collects no personal data, and I can't disable it. No cookies, no fingerprinting.</li>
          <li>This site was <strong>vibecoded</strong>. The code is AI-generated, but every piece of information, every recommendation, and every design choice was intentionally curated by me.</li>
          <li>This site is open to contributions. If you spot an error, have a better alternative, or want to improve a guide — reach out at <a href="mailto:contact@techfencing.com"><strong>contact@techfencing.com</strong></a> or open a PR on <a href="https://github.com/devdavv/TechFencing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>GitHub</strong></a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero-sm {
    padding: var(--space-12) 0 var(--space-6);
    text-align: center;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: rgba(10, 0, 0, 0.6);
  }

  :global(.page-title) {
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
  }

  .about-content {
    max-width: 750px;
  }

  .about-block {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }

  .about-block h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-block p {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .belief-list,
  .disclaimer-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .belief-list li,
  .disclaimer-list li {
    padding: var(--space-4) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(212, 84, 94, 0.08);
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .belief-list li:last-child,
  .disclaimer-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

</style>
